-- title:
--   The soft-threshold clipping function
-- statement:
--   For $\varepsilon\ge0$, the clipping function shrinks a real number towards $0$ by $\varepsilon$:
--   $$
--   \mathrm{clip}_\varepsilon(t)=\max(t-\varepsilon,0)+\min(t+\varepsilon,0).
--   $$
--
--   It vanishes on $[-\varepsilon,\varepsilon]$, equals $t-\varepsilon$ for $t\ge\varepsilon$ and $t+\varepsilon$ for $t\le-\varepsilon$, and is $1$-Lipschitz with $|t-\mathrm{clip}_\varepsilon(t)|\le\varepsilon$. It is used to give Lipschitz functions compact support.
